						(xy 0 0) (xy 0 1.27) (xy -1.016 1.905) (xy 0 2.54) (xy 1.016 1.905) (xy 0 1.27)
					)
					(stroke
						(width 0)
						(type default)
					)
					(fill
						(type none)
					)
				)
			)
			(embedded_fonts no)
		)
	)
	(text "7. Common ground for everything. GPIO32/33/25/26 are input-capable pins with no boot-strap restrictions."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 258 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0612ece0-0b43-4ef6-ac1d-2bd7d35e82f4")
	)
	(text "IDEA 8 - SELF-DIMMING STREET LIGHTS (ESP32 + WS2812B + 4 IR sensors + INA219)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 15 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3 3)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "06851225-a6b9-4248-950f-fa6560227991")
	)
	(text "6. Strip is one physical strip split in software into 5 lamp segments (e.g. 6 LEDs each). Do not draw more than ~3A: cap global brightness in code."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 252 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "18cdc43c-0047-4174-ab34-76160675ee7b")
	)
	(text "System-level wiring schematic using module symbols (not PCB footprints). Pins are joined by net labels of the same name."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3ee33015-0375-41ac-8cea-be1d7564a324")
	)
	(text "2. INA219 shunt is in series with the strip 5V rail: +5V_IN -> VIN+ ... VIN- -> +5V_LED. I2C address 0x40; BH1750 ADDR low = 0x23."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 228 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7dd196b5-3fe7-425f-8e83-a0e85b5333ec")
	)
	(text "5. FC-51 IR sensors are powered from 3V3 so their outputs are safe for the ESP32 GPIOs. Output is LOW when an object is detected. Tune the pot on each."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 246 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "93f839c6-4f5a-4869-959e-78572cf1d543")
	)
	(text "4. 74AHCT125 (14 pins): gate 1 shifts 3.3V data to 5V (1OE pin1 to GND = enabled, 1A pin2 in, 1Y pin3 out). Unused gates 2-4 have OE and A tied to GND (pins 4,5,9,10,12,13); their outputs stay open. VCC pin14, GND pin7, 0.1uF C2 close to the chip."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 240 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c938666d-5b17-4b34-aee7-67a31c0c76a2")
	)
	(text "NOTES"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 215 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "dae05226-4165-4c2a-ace1-4ade0805c781")
	)
	(text "3. 1000uF cap across the strip supply and the 330R series resistor protect the first WS2812B LED; keep the data wire short."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 234 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f0d63455-0e98-49c8-8dcb-8464b53604a6")
	)
	(text "1. ESP32 is powered from +5V_IN (before the INA219) so the INA219 measures only the LED strip, which is the load being optimised."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 222 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f41dae28-a505-4a82-86d1-742179a8dbed")
	)
